  "tagline": "The original Lucene search server: battle-tested, Apache-governed, now with GPU-accelerated vectors.",
  "description": "Solr is the Apache Software Foundation's search server built on Lucene, and it predates Elasticsearch by years. It is configuration-heavy but extremely capable: faceting, grouping, joins, streaming expressions, learning-to-rank and, since 9.x, dense vector search. Solr 10.0 (March 2026) moved to Java 21 and Lucene 10, added quantized vectors and cuVS GPU indexing, and trimmed legacy modules. It fits teams that want fully Apache-licensed, community-run enterprise search and are comfortable running ZooKeeper-backed SolrCloud clusters.",
